From: Zhibo Zhang <24061721@hdu.edu.cn>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:40:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] P19: the same number written another way must keep full
 reward

Adds a per-example probe for numeric false fails: a reference that is a plain
number is re-rendered as a value-identical form (36 -> 36.0, +36, 12,000,
U+2212 for negatives) and must still earn full reward. A grader that rejects
them reads the string instead of the number.

Docs: README/README.zh-CN table rows, draft.py description; the row is a lead
like P2 and joins NEEDS_JUDGEMENT. Tests: a string-matching grader is flagged
on rather than some variants, a numeric one is cleared, and the existing
strict-grader parametrisation allows P19 alongside P2.
